{
  "surface": "account-links",
  "route": "/account/links",
  "notes": "The owned-link list at rest (#941): the code chip, the status pill, the protected pill, the Hijri date pill and the destination the page draws for a link. `origin` is the code chip, because the page's frame and the app's frame are different heights and the design this contract owns is the row's own boxes. `capture` is the destination line, because its box is the width the row gives it on both clients and does not depend on whether the badges wrapped: the row's action toolbar is a later slice (#943) and is outside this contract. The destination's width is the row's width on the page and is measured; its height is one line of `text-[13px] leading-relaxed`. Widths of the code chip and the pills are left out deliberately - they are the run of the words and the glyphs, not a decision - and colours are left out too, because they are what the raster proves. The protected pill is drawn for a link the fixture gives a password, so the state records every pill the page's row draws. `bulk-bar` is the bar above the rows with its one fixture row selected (#942): the page's 44-high select-all, its 18-high checkbox, the count line and the four 30-high actions. The bar's height is measured because it is the wrap the page draws at 393 - select-all, the count and the spacer share the first line with clear and copy, and expiry and delete wrap to the second - and `capture` is the bar so the raster proves that wrap. The buttons' widths are left out: they are the run of the words and the glyphs, and the raster is what proves them.",
  "states": [
    {
      "name": "at-rest",
      "origin": "code",
      "capture": "destination",
      "elements": [
        {
          "name": "code",
          "web": {
            "selector": "[data-visual='link-row-code']"
          },
          "app": {
            "tag": "linksnap-row-code"
          },
          "properties": ["height", "fontSize", "fontWeight", "radius", "paddingTop", "paddingLeft"]
        },
        {
